    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "girth for a horse (OED s.v. girth n.1) | woven belt or band, placed around the body of a horse or other beast of burden and drawn tight, so as to secure a saddle or pack etc. upon its back (OED s.v. girth n.1 1a) | (gyrte (gyrthe) webbe) a woven material of which girths (a belt or band of leather or cloth, placed around the body of a horse or other beast of burden and drawn tight, so as to secure a saddle or pack etc. upon its back (OED s.v. girth n.^1 1a)) are made | woven material of which girths (for horses) are made | a belt or band of leather or cloth, placed around the body of a horse or other beast of burden and drawn tight, so as to secure a saddle or pack etc. upon its back (OED s.v. girth n.1 1a) | a belt or band of leather or cloth, placed around the body of a horse or other beast of burden and drawn tight, so as to secure a saddle or pack etc. upon its back (OED s.v. girth n.1 1a, garth2)" ;
